1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,035
Pump up a bicycle tyre, then watch
the little valve as the wheel turns.

2
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:07,985
Sometimes above the hub, sometimes below.

3
00:00:07,985 --> 00:00:10,877
Sometimes to the right,
sometimes to the left.

4
00:00:11,277 --> 00:00:15,784
Diya spotted this while Aarav was
fixing his front wheel after class.

5
00:00:16,134 --> 00:00:20,550
She asked: when the valve is below
the hub, is its height a minus number?

6
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:21,950
It is.

7
00:00:21,795 --> 00:00:26,653
And that one idea decides the sign
of every trigonometric function, in

8
00:00:26,653 --> 00:00:28,187
all four quadrants.

9
00:00:28,837 --> 00:00:29,887
Quick recall.

10
00:00:29,887 --> 00:00:34,190
Draw a circle of radius one,
with its centre at the origin O.

11
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:35,991
This is the unit circle.

12
00:00:36,391 --> 00:00:39,470
Turn an angle theta from
the positive x axis.

13
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:42,357
The arm ends at a point P on the circle.

14
00:00:42,757 --> 00:00:45,532
The x coordinate of P is cosine theta.

15
00:00:45,532 --> 00:00:47,811
The y coordinate is sine theta.

16
00:00:48,211 --> 00:00:50,481
So cosine tells you left or right.

17
00:00:50,481 --> 00:00:52,310
Sine tells you up or down.

18
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:53,890
Right and up are plus.

19
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,566
Left and down are minus.

20
00:00:56,216 --> 00:00:59,965
Now let P travel all the way
round, and watch the signs.

21
00:01:00,365 --> 00:01:03,619
First quadrant, theta
from zero to pi by two.

22
00:01:03,619 --> 00:01:05,763
P is to the right and above.

23
00:01:05,763 --> 00:01:08,001
Cosine is plus, sine is plus.

24
00:01:08,501 --> 00:01:11,373
Second quadrant, from pi by two to pi.

25
00:01:11,373 --> 00:01:13,108
P crosses to the left.

26
00:01:13,108 --> 00:01:16,022
Cosine turns minus, but sine stays plus.

27
00:01:16,522 --> 00:01:19,795
Third quadrant, from
pi to three pi by two.

28
00:01:19,795 --> 00:01:21,464
P is left and below.

29
00:01:21,464 --> 00:01:23,790
Cosine and sine are both minus.

30
00:01:24,290 --> 00:01:27,375
Fourth quadrant, three
pi by two to two pi.

31
00:01:27,375 --> 00:01:29,944
P is back on the right, but below.

32
00:01:29,944 --> 00:01:32,187
Cosine is plus, sine is minus.

33
00:01:32,687 --> 00:01:34,346
Now look at the sine graph.

34
00:01:34,346 --> 00:01:38,503
It stays above the axis for the first
half turn, and below it for the second

35
00:01:38,503 --> 00:01:39,403
half.

36
00:01:39,627 --> 00:01:43,715
The other four functions are built
from sine and cosine, so their signs

37
00:01:43,715 --> 00:01:44,615
follow.

38
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:45,642
Step one.

39
00:01:45,642 --> 00:01:48,388
Tangent is sine divided by cosine.

40
00:01:49,138 --> 00:01:50,038
Step two.

41
00:01:49,984 --> 00:01:54,747
When you divide, same signs give
plus, and opposite signs give minus.

42
00:01:55,497 --> 00:01:56,425
Step three.

43
00:01:56,425 --> 00:02:01,203
Sine and cosine have the same sign
only in the first and third quadrants.

44
00:02:01,203 --> 00:02:04,893
So tangent is plus there,
and minus in the other two.

45
00:02:05,643 --> 00:02:06,601
Step four.

46
00:02:06,601 --> 00:02:10,915
Cosecant is one over sine, so
it copies the sign of sine.

47
00:02:10,915 --> 00:02:12,544
Secant copies cosine.

48
00:02:12,544 --> 00:02:14,393
Cotangent copies tangent.

49
00:02:15,143 --> 00:02:16,260
Side by side.

50
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,971
Sixty degrees is in the first quadrant.

51
00:02:18,971 --> 00:02:23,450
Sine is about zero point eight
seven, and cosine is plus a half.

52
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:27,363
One hundred and twenty degrees
is in the second quadrant.

53
00:02:27,363 --> 00:02:28,883
The sine is the same.

54
00:02:28,883 --> 00:02:31,333
But the cosine flips to minus a half.

55
00:02:31,933 --> 00:02:33,866
Same height, opposite sides.

56
00:02:33,866 --> 00:02:35,760
The quadrant gives the sign.

57
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,489
Now you try.

58
00:02:37,489 --> 00:02:41,315
Is cosine of two hundred
degrees positive or negative?

59
00:02:41,315 --> 00:02:42,718
Pause and decide.

60
00:02:45,918 --> 00:02:46,818
Negative!

61
00:02:46,656 --> 00:02:51,125
Two hundred degrees is in the third
quadrant, where P is to the left of

62
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:52,025
O.

63
00:02:52,174 --> 00:02:56,637
A quick way to remember: start in the
first quadrant, and go anticlockwise.

64
00:02:57,037 --> 00:02:59,505
First quadrant, all six are plus.

65
00:02:59,505 --> 00:03:01,805
Second, only sine and cosecant.

66
00:03:01,805 --> 00:03:04,263
Third, only tangent and cotangent.

67
00:03:04,263 --> 00:03:06,563
Fourth, only cosine and secant.

68
00:03:06,963 --> 00:03:08,988
All, Sine, Tangent, Cosine.

69
00:03:08,988 --> 00:03:11,457
Or remember: All Students Take Coffee.

70
00:03:12,107 --> 00:03:13,212
Remember this.

71
00:03:13,212 --> 00:03:18,219
Going anticlockwise from the first
quadrant: All, Sine, Tangent, Cosine.

72
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:19,819
Quick one.

73
00:03:19,798 --> 00:03:22,697
Sine is negative, but tangent is positive.

74
00:03:22,697 --> 00:03:24,414
Which quadrant is P in?

75
00:03:24,414 --> 00:03:25,656
Pause and think.

76
00:03:28,856 --> 00:03:29,756
The third!

77
00:03:29,718 --> 00:03:32,323
Sine is minus in the third and fourth.

78
00:03:32,323 --> 00:03:34,977
Tangent is plus in the first and third.

79
00:03:34,977 --> 00:03:36,711
Only the third has both.

80
00:03:37,361 --> 00:03:39,096
Now, one worked example.

81
00:03:39,446 --> 00:03:43,700
Theta is in the second quadrant,
and sine theta is three fifths.

82
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,384
Find cosine and tangent.

83
00:03:45,884 --> 00:03:46,784
Step one.

84
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:51,488
P is on the unit circle, so cosine
squared plus sine squared is one.

85
00:03:52,238 --> 00:03:53,155
Step two.

86
00:03:53,155 --> 00:03:56,311
Cosine squared is
sixteen over twenty five.

87
00:03:56,311 --> 00:03:59,309
So cosine is plus or minus four fifths.

88
00:04:00,059 --> 00:04:00,974
Step three.

89
00:04:00,974 --> 00:04:04,771
In the second quadrant, P is
to the left of the centre.

90
00:04:04,771 --> 00:04:07,276
So cosine theta is minus four fifths.

91
00:04:08,026 --> 00:04:08,985
Step four.

92
00:04:08,985 --> 00:04:11,135
Tangent is sine over cosine.

93
00:04:11,135 --> 00:04:15,776
Three fifths divided by minus four
fifths is minus three quarters.

94
00:04:16,526 --> 00:04:19,460
The quadrant, not the
arithmetic, chose the sign.

95
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:21,575
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:21,925 --> 00:04:26,034
Many students think: in the third
quadrant, everything is negative.

97
00:04:26,034 --> 00:04:28,098
So tangent must be negative too.

98
00:04:28,498 --> 00:04:32,687
But tangent is sine over cosine,
and minus over minus is plus.

99
00:04:32,687 --> 00:04:36,716
At two hundred and twenty five
degrees, tangent is plus one.

100
00:04:37,366 --> 00:04:39,015
Where is this asked?

101
00:04:39,015 --> 00:04:44,331
In PUC exams and JEE Main: one ratio
and the quadrant are given, find the

102
00:04:44,331 --> 00:04:45,231
others.

103
00:04:45,661 --> 00:04:46,879
Exam level now.

104
00:04:46,879 --> 00:04:49,261
Find the value of this expression.

105
00:04:49,261 --> 00:04:50,530
Pause and solve.

106
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:57,452
The answer is B.

107
00:04:57,452 --> 00:04:58,352
Nineteen.

108
00:04:58,849 --> 00:05:01,772
Tangent is negative,
and cosine is positive.

109
00:05:01,772 --> 00:05:05,817
That only happens in the fourth
quadrant, so sine is negative.

110
00:05:06,317 --> 00:05:11,025
Tangent is minus five over twelve,
so think of a five, twelve, thirteen

111
00:05:11,025 --> 00:05:11,925
triangle.

112
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:17,354
So sine theta is minus five over
thirteen, and cosine theta is twelve over

113
00:05:17,354 --> 00:05:18,254
thirteen.

114
00:05:18,675 --> 00:05:22,939
The expression becomes minus five
plus twenty four, which is nineteen.

115
00:05:23,539 --> 00:05:24,998
Here is your recap.

116
00:05:24,998 --> 00:05:26,497
Screenshot this card.

117
00:05:29,697 --> 00:05:32,534
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:32,934 --> 00:05:33,834
One.

119
00:05:33,474 --> 00:05:37,065
In which quadrant are sine
and cosine both negative?

120
00:05:37,964 --> 00:05:38,864
Two.

121
00:05:38,501 --> 00:05:42,328
Is tangent of three hundred
degrees positive or negative?

122
00:05:43,228 --> 00:05:44,128
Three.

123
00:05:43,831 --> 00:05:47,243
Why does cosecant always
have the same sign as sine?

124
00:05:48,343 --> 00:05:52,918
Next time: the valve can never rise
higher than the wheel's radius.

125
00:05:52,918 --> 00:05:55,138
So how big can sine ever get?

126
00:05:55,138 --> 00:05:59,117
We find out in domain and range
of trigonometric functions.
